<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Baldwin I, Latin Emperor</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1172–1205</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Baldwin IX of Flanders, Baldwin VI of Hainaut, Baldwin I of Constantinople</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Baldwin I, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> Emperor, was count of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/flanders">Flanders</a> and Hainaut and a leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fourth-crusade">Fourth Crusade</a>. After the crusaders took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a> in 1204 he was elected the first emperor of the Latin Empire. In April 1205 he was defeated and captured by the Bulgarian tsar <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaloyan-of-bulgaria">Kaloyan</a> at Adrianople and died in captivity; his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-of-flanders">Henry of Flanders</a> succeeded him.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/baldwin-i-latin-emperor.jpg" alt="Baldwin I, Latin Emperor" width="238" height="395" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: maître de fauvel · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Baldwin_I_of_Constantinople.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
